    "problem_statement": "`run_pending()` function executes all jobs instead of only pending ones\n\n#### Description\n\nThe `run_pending()` function is executing all scheduled jobs regardless of whether they are actually pending or not. This breaks the intended behavior where only jobs that are due to run should be executed.\n\n#### Steps/Code to Reproduce\n\n```python\nimport schedule\nimport time\nfrom datetime import datetime\n\ndef job():\n    print(f\"Job executed at {datetime.now()}\")\n\n# Schedule a job to run every minute\nschedule.every().minute.do(job)\n\n# This should not execute the job immediately since it's not pending yet\nschedule.run_pending()\nprint(\"run_pending() called - job should not have run yet\")\n\n# Wait a bit and call again - still shouldn't run\ntime.sleep(30)  # 30 seconds, job scheduled for every minute\nschedule.run_pending()\nprint(\"run_pending() called again - job still shouldn't run\")\n```\n\nExpected behavior: The job should only execute when it's actually time for it to run (after a full minute has passed).\n\nActual behavior: The job executes immediately on every call to `run_pending()`, regardless of the schedule.\n\nThis affects any code that relies on `run_pending()` to only execute jobs when they are actually due, breaking the core scheduling functionality."
  }
